Task 2. Run the baseline evaluation
In this task, you establish the initial performance metrics of the coding agent.

Open a new terminal window within the Cloud Shell Editor, initialize virtual environment (.venv).
source .venv/bin/activate
Copied!
Execute the evaluation harness (eval.py) across all five tasks to generate the baseline results.
python eval.py
Copied!
If you re-run the evaluation harness a few times, you may notice that the results are flaky but on average less than half of all tasks are solved correctly. Your goal is to optimize this coding agent so that it reliably solves at least four of the five tasks.

Instead of rerunning the full evaluation, you can use the --task parameter to evaluate one specific task.
python eval.py --task <enter task_id>
Copied!
Verify that the evaluation run completes and creates a new run directory under runs/<timestamp>/.

You can see runs/<timestamp>/ folder in the EXPLORER panel in the Cloud Shell Editor should look like this:

evaluation timestamp runs 

A FAIL result tells you that the agent failed. It says nothing about why. In the next task you diagnose why the agent failed — the capability its harness was missing, or the wrong move it made — not just the bug hidden in the task.

